/* sql.Field ( qualifiedFieldName )
   Strips the table-occurrence prefix from a GetFieldName result,
   returning the bare field name for use in ExecuteSQL.

   Usage:
     "SELECT " & sql.Field ( GetFieldName ( PEOPLE::Name ) ) & " FROM ..."

   The call site wraps the field reference in GetFieldName.
   Custom function parameters are evaluated, so this function
   cannot call GetFieldName itself — that is a native function
   taking an unevaluated field reference. Passing the field
   directly (sql.Field ( PEOPLE::Name )) would hand this function
   the field's VALUE, not its name.

   Safety:
     A renamed field: GetFieldName tracks the new name automatically.
     A deleted field: the calculation shows <Field Missing>, a visible break.
     A renamed TO: FileMaker tracks TOs internally by id; GetFieldName
       returns the current TO name, and this function strips it either way.

   Requires: FileMaker 19 or later. No dependencies. */

Let (
    [
        _pos = Position ( qualifiedFieldName ; "::" ; 1 ; 1 )
    ] ;
    If ( _pos > 0 ;
        Middle ( qualifiedFieldName ; _pos + 2 ; Length ( qualifiedFieldName ) ) ;
        qualifiedFieldName
    )
)
